<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">Core Drain</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">Core Drain</ansi> is the Core Guardian's recharge ability. Over a two-round
windup its chest-cavity irises open and filaments of cold light reach
out; on release it tears vitality from everyone in the room and pours
it into its own core — healing the Guardian and building toward a
<ansi fg="command">Core Discharge</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow">Counterplay: </ansi>

  Like the discharge, the drain windup can be INTERRUPTED with a thrown
  <ansi fg="command">flashbang</ansi> or a disruption spell (<ansi fg="command">neural-stun</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">sensory-overload</ansi>,
  <ansi fg="command">kinetic-shove</ansi>). Interrupting a drain denies both the damage and the
  heal — AND the charge it would have fed the core. But interrupts are a
  limited resource: spend them on the drains, or save them for the
  discharge? That choice is the fight.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help core-discharge</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help throw</ansi>
